# Normalize line endings for a multi-platform repo.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with
# LF everywhere.  This matters beyond style: tools/ci_clone_rebrew.sh and the
# CI steps that sed it are shell scripts, and a CRLF-checked-out one dies on
# the stray \r as a syntax error, exactly as a #!/bin/sh fixture with CRLF
# fails as "bad interpreter".  All tooling here (python, node, java,
# browsers) reads LF fine, so forcing LF costs nothing and removes the whole
# CRLF-corruption class.
* text=auto eol=lf

# True binary assets — never normalize.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
